      },
      "lineNbr": 279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-03T00:55:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should never happen before startScanDone() right? Because here you unregister but register may not have been called. Is it possible stop is called before start done, and we get stop done first?",
      "revId": "b8d9ea1feac6b44ec64d0558eb93d5f672f41d5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b280cab_5e730324",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/NetworkScanRequestTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-04T03:52:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This would never happen since the scan request will only be stored before the \"start\" command is sent to the modem in method startNewScan(), and when stopping any scan, the first step is to compare the \"scanId\" with the stored requests. In another word, because the handler is single thread, you can not send \"stop\" command to the modem before the \"start\" command is sent, or else the \"stop\" command will fail",
      "parentUuid": "ac4ce195_f39f8a25",
      "revId": "b8d9ea1feac6b44ec64d0558eb93d5f672f41d5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b670e74_5f1de72e",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/NetworkScanRequestTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-05T13:35:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not referring to sending the start command. startScanDone() is called on start command confirmation from RIL. Can that be delayed and happen after we get stop confirmation? I agree it should not happen, but that\u0027s up to the modem implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "0b280cab_5e730324",
      "revId": "b8d9ea1feac6b44ec64d0558eb93d5f672f41d5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af203b4d_a398ab81",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/NetworkScanRequestTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-05T17:07:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we get the stop confirmation before we get the start confirmation, we will\n1. unregister the handler before it is registered, this is logically incorrect but fine because the RegistrantList will remove whatever can be found for that handler.\n2. We will register the handler but no one will unregister it, and now this is actually a problem. I added one more check in the  startScanDone() to make sure the scan is still live before we register the handler.",
      "parentUuid": "7b670e74_5f1de72e",
      "revId": "b8d9ea1feac6b44ec64d0558eb93d5f672f41d5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75c3bc7a_50889e45",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/NetworkScanRequestTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 312,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-03T00:55:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "no notification in case of interrupt?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 312,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 312,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "b8d9ea1feac6b44ec64d0558eb93d5f672f41d5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10fbfc36_a8f1b97e",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/NetworkScanRequestTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 312,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-04T03:52:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it is interrupted by higher priority request, the notice has been sent to the user when the \"interrupt\" command is sent to the modem, if the \"interrupt\" is caused by BinderDeath, we don\u0027t send any notice at all, that is why no notice will be sent inside interruptScanDone(), but according to different types of \"interrupt\", we may or may not notify.",
      "parentUuid": "75c3bc7a_50889e45",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 312,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 312,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "b8d9ea1feac6b44ec64d0558eb93d5f672f41d5f",
